  "assumptions": [
    "TIME/TOD are whole milliseconds and DATE/DT whole seconds; sub-unit nanoseconds are discarded by the vendor-unit conversions.",
    "TIME wrap-around at 2^32 ms is not simulated: values outside 0..2^32-1 ms keep their 64-bit value; conversions to 32-bit integers still yield the vendor's low 32 bits.",
    "Negative integers converted to TIME give negative durations (CODESYS TIME is unsigned)."
  ]
